# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# This repo is LF throughout -- every file predating it is LF -- but it is
# developed on Windows, where several ordinary tools rewrite a whole file to
# CRLF as a side effect of editing one line. Python's `open(path, "w")` does it
# silently by default; so do some editors.
#
# The damage is not to the code, which runs identically either way. It is to
# review: a one-line change comes back as "every line changed", which hides the
# actual edit and makes `git blame` useless for that file. Four files were
# committed that way during Phase 5 before this was noticed.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes git store LF regardless of what is on disk, so the
# mistake cannot reach a commit again no matter which tool made it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# EXCEPT reference/, which is VENDORED FROM UPSTREAM and must stay byte-identical
# to what was copied in. SCHEMA.md is the operational contract for the original
# app and CHANGELOG.md is its history; both arrived CRLF. Normalising them would
# rewrite every line of a document this port is supposed to diff against, and the
# porting rules say not to edit reference/ here at all. `-text` disables all
# line-ending conversion for them.
reference/** -text

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
